<script>
' Chapter 1/4 — router.navigate(path, [params], [skipInHistory]) / router.back() / router.params.* /
' router.appendBackJourneyData/updateBackJourneyData + router.backJourneyData.* — the ONE chapter in
' this app that genuinely needs router NESTING (see findings/router-demo-app.md and MainScene.thr's
' own top comment): a plain "list" screen with nowhere real to navigate wouldn't demonstrate params
' or backJourneyData surviving a real destroy-and-recreate round trip, so this route declares its own
' `children: [...]` in MainScene.thr's setRouting() — a "list" default child (ParamsListScreen.thr)
' and a "detail" child (ParamsDetailScreen.thr) reached from it.
'
' THIS component is a deliberately thin wrapper — no focusable content, no visible chrome of its own
' — exactly like apps/sample-app's Shell.thr is chrome-ful while its OWN mounted default child
' (HomeScreen.thr) is what the vacuum rule actually lands default-focus on. Here there's no
' persistent-menu chrome to show, so this wrapper carries nothing but the nested outlet itself;
' ParamsListScreen.thr's own default-focus="true" is what actually receives focus the first time this
' chapter is entered, exactly one level down.
scale field rootWidth: integer = 1280
scale field rootHeight: integer = 720

public function setup() {
  router.markReady()
}
</script>

<component>
<FlashTheaterRouterOutlet id="childOutlet" width="{rootWidth}" height="{rootHeight}" />
</component>
